{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it says, iron and copper.</b> That is, in his portion there shall be mountains of iron and copper. Or it comes to hint that his land shall be the lock of the land of Israel, and he shall have doors of copper and bars of iron, and the whole land locked by them. And the intent of this is that enemies shall not come into his land to plunder his oil from him, but rather he shall convey it from his land to other lands." "<b>And as your days, yourדבאך.</b> The opinion of Onkelos is that the word is inverted, and it is like דאבך, from the language of (Deuteronomy 28:65) ״דאבון נפש״, and this is what he translated: וכיומי עולימותך תוקפך — 'and as the days of your youth, your strength.' He explained וכימיך as referring to the days of youth, for they are called 'days' and are fit to be counted in the number of days, and דבאך as referring to the days of old age, which are days of דאבון נפש — anguish of soul — and suffering, and they are the years about which a man says, 'I have no pleasure in them.' <b>But according to the plain sense</b> of Scripture, the meaning of וכימיך דבאך is: 'and all your days your land shall flow with oil,' and it would be from the language of the Targum of (Leviticus 15) זב — דאיב. And so we find many expressions in the Torah that are Targum, such as (Genesis 31:47) ״יגר שהדותא״, which is the Targum of גלעד, and likewise ״ואתה מרבבות קדש״, and in the Prophets (Isaiah 21:12) ״אתא בקר וגם לילה אם תבעיון בעיו״, and likewise in the Writings (Psalms 9:5) ״כי עשית משפטי ודיני״, and furthermore (Job 16:19) ״הנה בשמים עדי ושהדי במרומים״, (ibid. 40) ״עצמיו אפיקי נחושה גרמיו כמטיל ברזל״, (Song of Songs 1:16) ״אף ערשנו רעננה״ — the Targum of מטה is ערסא — and the word combines both these languages, the holy language and the language of Targum. And so you will find in the composition of the holy Talmud that it contains these two languages, for Ravina and Rav Ashi followed the way of the Torah, which was given at Sinai. And in my opinion this matter has a root, for the name of HaShem, uniquely designated by His name, which is the holy language, and corresponding to the name of the angel, which is the Targum, is Metatron, and I am not permitted to elaborate in explanation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {1 "The Hebrew retains דבאך untranslated within the lemma and body as it is the word under analysis; Onkelos's Aramaic and all biblical quotations left in Hebrew script per protocol. The phrase ואתה מרבבות קדש appears without a biblical citation in the source; it echoes Deuteronomy 33:21 but is quoted here as an example of Targum-like Hebrew, left as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:31.721569787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}